^SAMPLE = GSM5822398
!Sample_title = A549-ACE2 Cas9CRISPRa infected population screen 1.construct
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM5822398
!Sample_status = Public on Jan 20 2022
!Sample_submission_date = Jan 17 2022
!Sample_last_update_date = Apr 30 2022
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = lung cells overexpressing ACE2
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: A549-ACE2
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: lung cells
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: overexpressing ACE2
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = perturbation type: CRISPR activation
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = crispr library: Cas9CRISPRa (CP1663)
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = infected with sars-cov-2?: YES
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = population: resistant_population_screen_1
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Infection with SARS-CoV-2 (BetaCoV/France/IDF0372/2020 isolate), MOI 0.005
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = Dulbecco's modified Eagle medium (DMEM) supplemented with 10% foetal bovine serum and penicillin/streptomycin, 37°C, 5%CO2
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = NucleoSpin Blood XL kit as per the manufacturer's instructions
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For PCR amplification, gDNA was divided into 100 μL reactions such that each well had at most 10 μg of gDNA. Plasmid DNA (pDNA) was also included at a maximum of 100 pg per well. Per 96 well plate, a master mix consisted of 150 μL DNA Polymerase (Titanium Taq; Takara), 1 mL of 10x buffer, 800 μL of dNTPs (Takara), 50 μL of P5 stagger primer mix (stock at 100 μM concentration), 500 μL of DMSO, and water to bring the final volume to 4 mL. Each well consisted of 50 μL gDNA plus water, 40 μL PCR master mix, and 10 μL of a uniquely barcoded P7 primer (stock at 5 μM concentration). PCR cycling conditions were as follows: an initial 1 min at 95 °C; followed by 30 s at 94 °C, 30 s at 52.5 °C, 30 s at 72 °C, for 28 cycles; and a final 10 min extension at 72 °C. PCR primers were synthesized at Integrated DNA Technologies (IDT). PCR products were purified with Agencourt AMPure XP SPRI beads according to manufacturer’s instructions (Beckman Coulter, A63880). Prior to sequencing the sample was quantitated by qPCR and diluted to 2nM. 5 µL of the  sample was then further diluted and denatured with 5 µL 0.1N NaOH and 490 µL HT1 buffer (Illumina). Samples were sequenced on a HiSeq2500 HighOutput (Illumina) with a 5% spike-in of PhiX.
!Sample_description = Supplemental_File_13_A549-ACE2_Act_SecondaryLibrary_Goujon.xlsx
!Sample_data_processing = Raw read counts were retrieved from sequencing data using PoolQ version 3.2.9-3.2.11
!Sample_data_processing = Read counts were log-normalized, then averaged across conditions if applicable
!Sample_data_processing = Log-fold changes were calculated relative to pDNA
!Sample_data_processing = Fit a natural cubic spline between the control and infected conditions and calculated residuals from this spline (anchors package)
!Sample_data_processing = Z-scored residuals at the guide-level (anchors package)
!Sample_data_processing = Averaged across guides and conditions to get gene-level average z-score (anchors package)
!Sample_data_processing = Applied filter based on number of guides per gene then ranked genes where a rank of 1 was assigned to the top pro-viral hit
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: NCBI GRCh38 primary assembly
